    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i keep getting this SettingWithCopyWarning in my notebook when i try to add a new column to a dataframe after filtering it. can u explain why this happens and how i actually fix it? i dont want to just suppress the warning, i want to know the right way to do it.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This `SettingWithCopyWarning` pops up because pandas is unsure if you are modifying a view of a slice (a copy of the original data) or the original DataFrame itself. It's a warning, not an error, but it means your changes might not stick where you expect them to. To fix this properly, you should explicitly create a copy of the filtered DataFrame before adding the new column, like this: `df_filtered = df[condition].copy()`. This tells pandas, \"I want a brand new, independent DataFrame here,\" which prevents the ambiguity.",
